<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Danish long yields up to 7.34 pct in 97.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Danish long yields up to 7.34 pct in 97.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish bond yields will climb steadily over the next 12 months, a Reuter consensus poll of 17 economists indicated on Monday.</p>
<p>An average of forecasts showed the benchmark eight percent bond due 2006, currently yielding around 6.80 percent, up at 7.10 pct by the end of this year.</p>
<p>By end-March 1997 the benchmark was seen yielding 7.23 percent, rising to an average 7.34 percent by end-September 1997. The 10-year yield gap with Germany was expected to widen from 80 basis points today to 86 b.p. three months ahead, 83 b.p.in six months, narrowing to 80 b.p. again in 12 months on average.</p>
<p>Three-month rates would dip from 3.70 percent now to an average 3.68 percent in three months, rising to 3.78 percent in six months and 4.13 percent next September, the poll said.</p>
